# Implementation Plan: World-Class UI/UX Refinement

This plan addresses the feedback regarding typography inconsistencies, contrast errors, and the general "feel" of the Icarus platform. The goal is to move from a "good" first iteration to a "Senior-level" premium experience.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Dynamic Navbar Behavior**: We will implement a scroll-listener to transition the Navbar from transparent to a "Frosted Crystal" glassmorphism when scrolling past the hero. 
> **Typography Shift**: I propose using a semi-bold serif for major headings and increasing body text size/line-height for better "breathability".

## Proposed Changes

### [Component] Global Design System & Typography
#### [MODIFY] [globals.css](file:///c:/Users/hp/Desktop/icarus/src/app/globals.css)
*   Update serif heading tokens to use `font-weight: 600` and `letter-spacing: -0.02em`.
*   Increase base line-height for body text from 1.5 to 1.7.
*   Refine `glass` and `glass-dark` utilities with higher `backdrop-blur` (16px+) and a `0.5px` stroke for the "Frosted Crystal" look.
*   Add a `section-padding` utility that uses `clamp` for responsive, generous whitespace.

